course: dictionary
lesson: 8231
title: Revision: going over what you learned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Revision means going over what you learned before, so that you remember it well. Many people do revision before a test. «Worrying more does not make revision work better.» Worrying fills your mind, but going over facts and practising them is what helps you remember.
explain: Revision can also mean a change made to improve a piece of writing or a plan. A revision of my story is a better version after I have fixed it. In a maths lesson, a revision set is a group of problems from earlier lessons that you practise again.
explain: In a revision set the problems are mixed up, so read each one on its own and decide what it asks. «Revision games and quizzes are real practice, and they make it less stressful.» Those are good ways to revise.
fact: Revision means going over what you learned before so you remember it well.
fact: «Revision» is used mostly in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand; in the USA people say «review».
fact: A revision can also be a change made to improve a piece of writing or a plan.
fact: «Making a revision plan with AI is a good use, as long as you then follow the plan yourself.»
fact: Revision is a noun: one revision, and more than one revisions.
exercise: Lily spends the evening going over her spelling words before Friday's test. What is she doing? | *Revision, going over what she learned before | Taking a new test | Painting a picture | Revising a story to make it better
exercise: «Making a revision plan with AI is a good use, as long as you then follow the plan yourself.» What is the most important part of this? | Losing the plan | Asking the AI to do everything | Not making any plan at all | *Following the plan yourself
exercise: In a revision set, the problems are mixed up. What should you do with each one? | Copy the answer from the lesson before | *Read it on its own and decide what it asks | Skip them all | Do only the first one
test: The word «revision» is used mostly in the UK. What do people in the USA say instead? | Revise | *Review | Remember | Rehearsal
test: What is the plural of revision? | revisiens | revisioned | *revisions | revisionses
exam: «Revision games and quizzes are real practice, and they make it less stressful.» What do these sentences tell you about revision? | It is only for grown-ups | It is a waste of time | It always means changing a story | *It is real practice that can feel less stressful
